{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790351500,"nonce":"sr6vJdoYuOsgKL1fIEsBtwgg3Z4=","title":"zynml build: ahead-of-time executables through the same frontend as zynml run","message":"ZynML has no AOT command; the only route is `zyntax compile`, whose thin lowering resolves no imports, passes no plugin signatures and skips impl blocks, so no program that imports the prelude builds. Add `zynml build -o \u003cexe\u003e` that reuses what `zynml run` does (import resolution, prelude, plugin signatures, the HIR pipeline), then emits an object through the LLVM pipeline for the target CPU and links it with the stdlib plugins built as linked-into-host static archives. An AOT build then gives the same output as the JIT for any program the JIT runs.\n\nCovers or depends on:\n- e0f4d4af72eda1f6336af3b865b6715114db6cd1ca4ee466a8a66edc1e829fd9 (the CLI's thin lower_to_hir)\n- 36aa93b6dee9ff5ff902aa1cd3f979b6ad02fe040d4cdfda45d2b290f9aedc1c (plugin symbol names and colliding archives)\n- e311f718e613c36a216587260dd2c77ebc89e74b5e179f966c891d2aa6b78982 (no LLVM or HIR optimisation in AOT)\n- 5558584fa8dd059b27d5c043d5d9f49e92bb8b1f039b93c863c90cc4d8398fef (void main exit status)\n- 018d88f114e47bd5c04dca1a77a4a27899d253d6f17f8e3e8ac585ee977f1f57 (closures in the LLVM backend)","files":null}]}